  "configuration_id": "config_041",
  "reason": "The dominant finding from 5 experiments is that scvi_n200 as RNA encoder (config_021, acc=0.706) vastly outperforms scgpt (~0.52-0.54), and avgpool+weighted fusion is the best aggregation/fusion combination tested. However, all scvi_n200 experiments so far use imagenet_vit_l; the image encoder dimension is completely unexplored for this strong RNA encoder. config_041 (scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) is a clean single-variable test that changes only the image encoder from imagenet_vit_l to resnet50 while keeping all other parameters at their best-known settings. This directly tests whether the image encoder is a bottleneck or whether imagenet_vit_l is already near-optimal. With 4 experiments remaining after this one, clarifying the image encoder choice is critical: if resnet50 matches or beats imagenet_vit_l, it opens additional combinations; if it underperforms, we can confidently exploit imagenet_vit_l in the remaining budget. This is the highest-information, lowest-risk next step given the strong evidence for scvi_n200+avgpool+weighted."
}

